.TH SPARKY-STEREO-THROW 1 2026-11-25 "sparky-stereo-throw 0.1.0" "Sparky Stereo OS"
.SH NAME
sparky-stereo-throw \- throw the desktop to Google Cast devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sparky-stereo-throw list
.br
.B sparky-stereo-throw throw
.I id
.RB [ \-\-wait
.IR seconds ]
.br
.B sparky-stereo-throw stop
.I id
.br
.B sparky-stereo-throw info
.I id
.br
.B sparky-stereo-throw volume
.I id
.IR level | \-
.RB [ mute | unmute ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command of the Throw service (org.sparky.Throw on the session bus). \fBlist\fR prints the Cast devices found on
the network as JSON: identity, name, model, what the model name tells, address, the mode a Throw uses and the state of
its Throw. \fBthrow\fR starts a Throw: the device becomes one more screen of KWin and plays its picture; with
\fB\-\-wait\fR the command waits for the device to play (exit 0) or for the failure (exit 1, the reason printed).
\fBstop\fR ends it. \fBinfo\fR prints what the device says about itself without an account (its setup information and
its receiver's status). \fBvolume\fR sets the device's volume (0 to 1, or \- to leave it) and mute, read back from the
device.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sparky-stereo-throwrc
[Device][\fIid\fR] Mode=\fIW\fRx\fIH\fR@\fIHz\fR overrides the mode of the device table for that device.
.TP
.I /usr/share/sparky-stereo-throw/devices.json
The device table: what each model plays.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Throw page in System Settings; the 3D format and eye swap of a network screen are in Display Settings.
